// ContextMod Devvit — example: URL-dedupe repost rule in DRY-RUN mode.
//
// Watch for reposts of the same URL within a 30-day window WITHOUT
// firing any actions. Use this when first deploying a repost rule to
// see what would have been flagged before promoting to live remove.
//
// The repost rule writes a seen-marker (`cm:{sub}:repost:url:{hash}`,
// 30d TTL, atomic SET NX per Codex H7) on first sight, then trips on
// the second sight. With `dryRun: true` on the remove action, the
// Observatory shows the would-have-fired entry with the diamond marker
// (◆) and no live Reddit side-effect.
//
// Reference: ../README.md "Config schema" + src/schema/app.schema.json.
//
// Schema notes:
//   - `repost` rule shipped Phase 2 (promoted from Phase 4). URL-mode only;
//     image-mode is Phase 4.7 deferred.
//   - `dryRun: true` on a per-action level ELEVATES to dry-run (Codex H1 —
//     global config.dryRun is authoritative; per-action can't demote).
//   - Fail-OPEN on Redis outage: if Redis is unreachable, the rule does NOT
//     trip (mod doesn't want false positives when storage hiccups).
{
  runs: [
    {
      name: 'repost-watch',
      checks: [
        {
          name: 'url-dedupe-30d',
          combinator: 'OR',
          filters: { authorIs: { isMod: false } },
          rules: [
            {
              kind: 'repost',
              name: 'url-30d',
              windowDays: 30,
            },
          ],
          actions: [
            { kind: 'remove', dryRun: true },
            { kind: 'report', reason: 'Repost (dry-run watching)' },
          ],
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
}
